   "key": "architecture",
   "title": "Architecture Walkthrough",
   "position": 1,
   "status": "ready",
   "kind": "backbone",
   "target_minutes": 5.0,
   "content": {
    "summary": "This section walks through the internal module structure and internal utilities of the Requests repository.",
    "blocks": [
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Architecture Walkthrough",
      "level": 2
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Requests library is structured into several core modules located under the src/requests directory [E1]. This section explores the module structure and internal utilities that power the repository."
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Module Structure",
      "level": 3
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The codebase is divided into multiple Python files handling specific responsibilities, such as authentication handlers in auth.py, connection utilities in utils.py, and models representing primary objects [E2, E3, E8]."
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Internal Utilities",
      "level": 3
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Internal helper functions that depend on extremely few external helpers are located in _internal_utils.py [E1]. These include string conversion helpers and header validation regex definitions [E1, E6]."
     },
     {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def to_native_string(string, encoding=\"ascii\"):\n    if isinstance(string, builtin_str):\n        out = string\n    else:\n        out = string.decode(encoding)\n\n    return out",
      "path": "src/requests/_internal_utils.py",
      "start_line": 25,
      "caption": "to_native_string helper function"
     },
     {
      "type": "diagram",
      "diagram_id": "dg:657bac3b64933f0a",
      "caption": "Module dependencies"
     }
    ]
