  {
   "key": "deployment",
   "title": "How to Run or Deploy",
   "position": 2,
   "status": "ready",
   "kind": "backbone",
   "target_minutes": 4.0,
   "content": {
    "summary": "This guide section details how the Requests library is tested locally and via GitHub Actions CI configuration.",
    "blocks": [
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "How to Run or Deploy",
      "level": 2
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Requests library uses pytest for running its test suites [E8]. Contributors are expected to run the tests locally to confirm they pass before submitting any code [E1]."
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Running Tests Locally",
      "level": 3
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "You can run tests using the pytest framework or via setup.py integration [E8]. The project includes various certificates for testing specific behaviors such as mTLS and expired certificates [E3, E4]."
     },
     {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "bash",
      "code": "make clean\nmake all",
      "path": "tests/certs/expired/README.md",
      "start_line": 6,
      "caption": "Regenerating test certificates if needed"
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Continuous Integration with GitHub Actions",
      "level": 3
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Automated testing is configured using GitHub Actions workflows, specifically under the Tests workflow [E6], which triggers on pushes and pull requests [E11]."
     },
     {
      "type": "diagram",
      "diagram_id": "dg:77d2d8d1dd27fedf",
      "caption": "Deployment topology"
     }
    ]
   },
