   "content": {
    "summary": "This guide section explores the core subsystem of Requests, detailing how HTTP sessions and requests are implemented and managed.",
    "blocks": [
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Requests Core Subsystem",
      "level": 2
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The core subsystem of Requests centers around managing state, configuration, and connections via session objects, and dispatching HTTP methods through a unified interface [E1, E8]."
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "HTTP Sessions and Configuration",
      "level": 3
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Session class provides cookie persistence, connection-pooling via urllib3, and configuration defaults across multiple requests [E1, E8]. When initialized, a Session sets up default headers, hooks, proxies, and connection adapters for HTTP and HTTPS protocols [E3]."
     },
     {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "class Session(SessionRedirectMixin):\n    __attrs__ = [\n        \"headers\",\n        \"cookies\",\n        \"auth\",\n        \"proxies\",\n        \"hooks\",\n        \"params\",\n        \"verify\",\n        \"cert\",\n        \"adapters\",\n        \"stream\",\n        \"trust_env\",\n        \"max_redirects\",\n    ]",
      "path": "src/requests/sessions.py",
      "start_line": 356,
      "caption": "Session attributes for persistence and configuration"
     },
     {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Executing HTTP Methods",
      "level": 3
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The request method on a Session constructs a Request object, prepares it, merges environment settings, and sends it to return a Response object [E2]."
     },
     {
      "type": "qa",
      "question": "How do session-level parameters interact with method-level parameters?",
      "answer": "Any dictionaries passed to a request method are merged with session-level values, where method-level parameters override session parameters but are not persistently stored across requests [E8].",
      "kind": "repository"
     }
    ]
   },
